<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia Q1 crude output at 625,000 bpd - Ecopetrol.</title>
<headline>Colombia Q1 crude output at 625,000 bpd - Ecopetrol.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia produced a daily average of 625,000 barrels of crude oil in the first quarter of 1997, though production slipped to an average of 605,500 bpd in March, the state oil company Ecopetrol said on Friday.</p>
<p>Ecopetrol in a statement gave no reason for the drop in March.</p>
<p>It said an overall trend toward higher production should allow Colombia to export more than 620,000 bpd in 1998.</p>
<p>((-- Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
